==General election==
===Candidates===
*[[Pro-Life (politician)|Marvin Richardson]] (unendorsed [[Constitution Party (United States)|Constitution]]) – [[Organic farming|organic]] [[strawberry]] [[farmer]]<ref name="butts">{{Cite news | last = Butts | first = Mike | title = No 'Pro-Life' allowed on ballot | newspaper = Idaho Press-Tribune | date = 2006-04-06 | url = http://www.idahopress.com/articles/2006/04/06/news/news2.txt | access-date = 2006-01-13 | archive-date = 2008-09-19 | archive-url = https://web.archive.org/web/20080919040338/http://www.idahopress.com/articles/2006/04/06/news/news2.txt | url-status = dead }}</ref>  and sawmill owner
*[[Jerry Brady]] ([[Democratic Party (United States)|Democratic]]), newspaper publisher and [[Idaho gubernatorial election, 2002|2002]] Democratic nominee for governor
*Ted Dunlap ([[Libertarian Party (United States)|Libertarian]])
*[[Butch Otter]] ([[Republican Party (United States)|Republican]]), U.S. Congressman, former [[Lieutenant Governor of Idaho]]

===Controversy===
A candidate legally named Marvin Pro-Life Richardson filed suit to force the state to print his full legal on the ballots, as filed in campaign paperwork. The Secretary of State stated that ballots themselves are supposed to be neutral, not political billboards, and declined the request.<ref>[http://www.idahopress.com/articles/2006/04/06/news/news2.txt No ‘Pro-Life’ allowed on ballot] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080919040338/http://www.idahopress.com/articles/2006/04/06/news/news2.txt |date=2008-09-19 }}, retrieved 12oct2006</ref>  In September 2006 he changed his legal name to simply "Pro-Life" in an attempt to force the issue.  However, the ballots went to the printer naming "Marvin Richardson" as the Constitution Party candidate.  The party later disavowed his candidacy resulting in a candidate without a name, and without a party, appearing on the ballot.<ref>[http://novotewasted.com/candidates/prolife.html  ‘Pro-Life’ Failed to receive the Idaho CP Certification For Candidacy], retrieved 12oct2006</ref>

